@startuml
' Diagram author: Eethanzyj.
' Depicted storage persistence implementation: WillChin484848 (PR #42).
' Original capacity feature: Kaishhhh.
title Capacity restoration
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
hide footbox

participant ":Duke" as Duke
participant "storage:Storage" as Storage
participant "orders:OrderList" as Orders

note over Duke, Orders
  Successful startup with an existing, valid save file.
end note
activate Duke
Duke -> Storage : load()
activate Storage
create Orders
Storage -> Orders : new OrderList()
activate Orders
deactivate Orders
note over Storage, Orders
  The initial capacity is 5.
  Storage reads and validates the saved lines.
end note
opt file contains # dailyCapacity=3
  Storage -> Orders : setDailyCapacity(3)
  activate Orders
  deactivate Orders
end
opt invalid capacity setting
  Storage -> Orders : setDailyCapacity(5)
  activate Orders
  deactivate Orders
  Storage -> Storage : warn user; retain valid orders
end
ref over Storage, Orders : Restore records and their IDs.
Storage --> Duke : orders
deactivate Storage
note over Duke, Storage
  Corrupted orders or unreadable files throw IllegalStateException.
  Invalid capacity alone warns and uses 5.
  For those errors, Duke reports the failure and stops before the CLI runs.
end note
deactivate Duke
@enduml
